The R implementation is separately written for groundtruth. Gaussian linear
study and summary semantics follow the public GroundTruth.jl at
https://github.com/itchyshin/GroundTruth.jl, commit
3738bfe340fff62ec1afb0a78f0101babe79fbd7 (Shinichi Nakagawa, 2026).

Frozen test fixtures rep1-data.csv and rep1-julia.csv are copied verbatim from
results/linear at that commit. Their SHA256 hashes and comparison tolerances
are pinned in tests/testthat/fixtures/freeze.json before numerical checks.
The private unpublished LMM branch is not the numerical reference.

R's random-number algorithm and stream allocation are versioned separately.
Agreement on paired data does not imply equal R/Julia random draws or prove
simulation calibration.
